  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-24: "Continue with next tasks". Issue #3014 (read it in full: gh issue view 3014) and DI-164 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md.

Task 204 (PR #3011) made `SignalClosureService.ReadPoliciesNotInForceAsync` page through every Off or Inactive policy; `ClosePoliciesNotInForceAsync` then sends one Signal query per such policy. ebilling task 117 switches record rules Off on every core-record delete, so that count grows without bound while most of those policies have no open Signals. `SignalReevaluationJob.MaxRunDuration` is 2 h. Entry points (search by name; origin/master e70ff38894): `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalClosureService.cs` `ClosePoliciesNotInForceAsync` (~161), `ReadPoliciesNotInForceAsync` (~200, also used with includeBilling:false at ~195 by the preview/sweep path), `CloseAsync`; `SignalReevaluationJob.cs` call site.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse SDK QueryExpression / LinkEntity paging, the ontology nightly re-evaluation job.</role>
  <goal>The nightly close's Dataverse calls scale with the number of not-in-force policies that still have open Signals, not with all not-in-force policies; which Signals are closed, and how, is unchanged.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Suggested direction from the issue (a hypothesis; check it): one paged query over open sprk_signal rows linked to sprk_policy where the policy is not in force under D-170 (Off, or Inactive; billing included for the close), grouped by policy, then the existing per-policy close on the Signals read. The preview and the sweep share `ReadPoliciesNotInForceAsync(includeBilling: false)`: either give the close its own selection and leave theirs unchanged, or prove both still work with tests. Read task 204's POML and notes (tasks/204-*.poml, notes/task-204-notes.md) and `git log -5` on both files first; ebilling-r1 merges into Signals code (run /conflict-check). A Signal linked to a deleted policy is a different sweep (CloseSignalsOfDeletedPoliciesAsync): leave it alone.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">D-170 (which policies are not in force) unchanged; D-120 (resolvedon = lastevaluated in the same update) unchanged; D-61 (never stamp an unchanged Signal) unchanged; task 204: a truncated read is reported and fails the run, including for the new query.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Closure reason codes, telemetry names and the job's outcome shape unchanged; secure-child Signals are closed exactly as today (no new skip, D-38).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run `--filter "FullyQualifiedName~Signals"` (includes contract baselines).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs fresh master in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface or DI registration; private helpers in SignalClosureService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Call-count test fails on origin/master: many Off policies (for example 500) with open Signals on few (for example 3) → Signal-read calls bounded by pages of the open-Signal query plus the closes, not per policy. Must-not-fire: an Off policy with open Signals still closes them all with the same reason; an in-force policy's Signals are untouched; a truncated read still fails the run; existing SignalClosure and SignalReevaluation tests pass unmodified.</constraint>
  </constraints>
