  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read #3014, task 204's POML and notes, both entry files; count today's calls on the fake for N Off policies; record in notes/task-209-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Failing call-count test and the must-not-fire controls.</step>
    <step order="3">Replace the per-policy discovery with one paged open-Signal query linked to not-in-force policies; keep the per-policy close and truncation reporting.</step>
    <step order="4">Filtered tests (SignalClosure, SignalReevaluation, Signals), full ArchTests, BFF build, publish-size delta; record after counts.</step>
    <step order="5">PR to master, body "Closes #3014"; notes in notes/task-209-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">With many not-in-force policies and open Signals on only a few, the close's Signal-read calls do not grow with the number of not-in-force policies (counted on the fake); the test fails on origin/master.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every open Signal of a not-in-force policy is still closed with the same reason, resolvedon and telemetry; in-force policies' Signals are untouched; unchanged Signals are not stamped; a truncated read still fails the run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The preview and sweep paths behave as before (unchanged or proven by tests); existing SignalClosure and SignalReevaluation tests pass unmodified; build, filtered tests and full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>The fix changes which Signals are closed, needs a schema or index change, a new service, or changes the preview/sweep results: STOP and report.</trigger>
